// Records the assignment of a filament preset to the only slot of a printer, where the assignment also switches
// the filament tab and its unsaved-changes prompt applies. Slot 1 is assigned through each route: a pick in its
// selector in the sidebar (its list opened with click and the row clicked), the select_preset tool, and the
// plugin API's orca.host.preset.filament.begin_update(1, name) run from run_script; for an ordinary change and
// for a change to a support filament of another type, without and with unsaved changes in the edited filament
// preset (the tool's preset_changes values and none; the prompt answered each way, counted, and read while it is
// open). Then the plugin API's forms that name no preset. Each case starts from fixtures/ops_presets.py's
// sentinels and reads what the call left once queued events have settled. The flush calculation stays "All":
// with one slot the flushing volumes matrix has no entry to recalculate. Run it on a freshly launched app with
//   tools/mcp/orca_mcp.py run-replay tools/mcp/tests/ops_assign_filament_preset_one_slot.json --out <dir>
